{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Managing the Restaurant", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Service With a Smile", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe emotions and feelings in present and past situations in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.  ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals to Express Annoyance: Will and Would", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use modals to express annoyance or disapproval, or to describe a particular behavior. <br/>You use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> or <span class=\"italic\">would</span> to express annoyance and criticize people's behavior or habits.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span> can be used to describe habits or things that are true. <br/>Example: <span class=\"italic\">Every day, Dan <span class=\"strong\">will</span> come to our restaurant and greet all our customers personally.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">At school Dan <span class=\"strong\">would</span> always follow the teacher's instructions.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> or <span class=\"italic\">would</span> to criticize people's behavior and habits and express annoyance at a person or a situation. <br/>Example: <span class=\"italic\">The washing machine <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> start! </span><br/><span class=\"italic\">The restaurant is so much quieter without Mike. He <span class=\"strong\">would</span> really ruin the atmosphere!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> with an if-clause to suggest disapproval.<br/>Example: <span class=\"italic\">If you <span class=\"strong\">will</span> complain so much, I'm not surprised customers are giving you such low ratings!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We will stand straight, not slouch, and smile!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If she will stop doing bizarre things, we should have no problems! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She would be the one causing issues. It's so like her!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "When and If", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">when</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> if </span> to talk about conditions that will be fulfilled before a situation can happen. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Real Conditional</span> to talk about things you normally do in real-life situations. <br/>You use<span class=\"italic\"> when</span> with the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect </span>to talk about a condition that needs to be completed before another one can occur.You use both<span class=\"italic\"> if </span> and <span class=\"italic\">when</span> in the <span class=\"strong\">Present Real Conditional</span>. <br/>For example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If</span> there are other areas that need improving, I usually like to hear from my staff about it.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">When</span> suggests that something happens regularly.<br/>For example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">When</span> I have a day off from work, I like to go to the mall.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Notice the structure of this type of conditional: <br/>If/When ... Simple Present ... , ... Simple Present ...", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">when</span> with the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> to suggest that something needs to happen before something else can happen. In that context, <span class=\"italic\">when</span> has the meaning of <span class=\"italic\">as soon as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">after</span>, <span class=\"italic\">until</span>. <br/>For example: <span class=\"italic\">We'll get started <span class=\"strong\">when</span> everyone <span class=\"strong\">has arrived</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you all settle down, we can start. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If everyone has taken a seat, we'll get started.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When we are on the restaurant floor, we smile. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If we wait tables with efficiency, we maximize sales. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to float around", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be \u200bdiscussed by a lot of \u200bpeople", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a result, there are some not so pleasant reviews floating around online. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in a meeting about customer service. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "refresher ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an activity that revises or updates one's skills or knowledge ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: So today's staff meeting is a refresher on customer service. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to touch base on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to talk briefly about", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There's a lot we will touch base on. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to maximize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to increase something as much as possible ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We must maximize our sales. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "primary  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "most important ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is important that everyone realizes that their primary job is connecting with the guests. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cause", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something happen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She would be the one causing issues. It's so like her. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a classmate, brainstorm the qualities of  good customer and  bad customer service. Consider different types of customer service, such as face-to-face or on the phone.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a chart with these qualities written in point form or complete sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your chart in groups. Do you share similar ideas with others in the group? What influenced your ideas? Do any of your classmates have experience helping customers? ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss the conditions that can lead to bad customer service. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share personal stories when you think you've been a bad customer or have received bad customer service.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I work with a classmate to brainstorm the qualities of good customer service.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a chart to show these qualities. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my ideas in groups.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share personal stories related to customer service.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": 